{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceConstable-29-Nov-2023-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 15, "tagged_count": 15, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "6 boys can complete a work in 18 hours. In how many hours will 16 boys complete the same work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "group-work", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "What is the remainder obtained when a prime number greater than 7 is divided by 6?", "options": [{"text": "3 or 5", "added": false}, {"text": "1 or 5", "added": false}, {"text": "2 or 3", "added": false}, {"text": "2 or 5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "The monthly income of Amara is ₹80,200. If her income is decreased by 11%, then find her new monthly income (in ₹).", "options": [{"text": "71,250", "added": false}, {"text": "71,500", "added": false}, {"text": "71,820", "added": false}, {"text": "71,378", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "On a certain sum of money, the difference between the compound interest for a year payable half-yearly, and the simple interest for a year is ₹729. If the rate of interest in both the cases is 6%, then the sum is:", "options": [{"text": "₹8,50,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,90,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹8,10,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹8,30,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "fractions-decimals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "If the average of 5 consecutive even numbers is 70, then the largest even number is:", "options": [{"text": "70", "added": false}, {"text": "74", "added": false}, {"text": "68", "added": false}, {"text": "66", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0.59", "added": false}, {"text": "0.70", "added": false}, {"text": "0.69", "added": false}, {"text": "0.60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "The area of a triangle is 182 cm2 and the length of one of its sides is 28 cm. What is the length of the perpendicular line segment drawn to this side of the triangle from the opposite vertex (in cm)?", "options": [{"text": "6.5", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "What number must be added to each term of ratio 3 : 5 so that it may equal to 5 : 6?", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "The price of an article is first decreased by 25% and then increased by 35%. If the resulting price is ₹405, what was the original price of the article?", "options": [{"text": "₹350", "added": false}, {"text": "₹300", "added": false}, {"text": "₹450", "added": false}, {"text": "₹400", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹50,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹45,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹60,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹55,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "successive-transactions", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "A train travelling at a speed of 54 km/h catches another train travelling in the same direction and then leaves it 70 m behind in 14 seconds. The speed of the second train is:", "options": [{"text": "54 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "36 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "24 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "48 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "The annual instalment of ₹750 in 5 years at 5% per annum simple interest will discharge a debt of ______.", "options": [{"text": "₹4,025", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,215", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,937.5", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,125", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-instalments", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "The marked price of a commodity was ₹2,875. The seller offered a discount of 8% on its sale and still made a profit of 15%. What was the cost price (in ₹) of the commodity?", "options": [{"text": "2248.25", "added": false}, {"text": "2375", "added": false}, {"text": "2275.75", "added": false}, {"text": "2300", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}]}